          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Perry-Schwarz Lagrangian
            is
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+field"} self-dual higher gauge field
            in 6d and/or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+model"} Green-Schwarz sigma model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            to 5
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
          %p
            The construction is closely related to the following basic fact relating
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+3-forms"} differential 3-forms
            on 6d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Maxwell+theory"} D=5 Maxwell theory
          %div
            %h3#relation_between_5d_maxwell_theory_and_selfdual_3forms_in_6d Relation between 5d Maxwell theory and self-dual 3-forms in 6d
            %p
              Consider 5d- and 6d-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              equipped with global
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthonormal+basis"} orthonormal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+charts"} coordinate charts
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi κ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x^\kappa\}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x^\alpha\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry"} isometric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedding
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 4
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↪
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %msub
                                  %mi ι
                                  %mn 5
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 5
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi κ
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 3
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 4
                            %mphantom
                              %mo ,
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi α
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 3
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 4
                            %mo ,
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;
                    \\mathbb{R}^{4,1}
                    \&amp;\overset{\;\;\;\iota_5\;\;\;}{\hookrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{R}^{5,1}
                    \\\
                    \\kappa = &amp;   0, 1, 2, 3, 4\phantom{,}
                    \\\
                    \\alpha = &amp; 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, &amp;&amp; 5
                    }
            %p
              With this notation, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback of differential forms
              along this embedding is notationally implicit.
            %p
              Now any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+3-form"} differential 3-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 5
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{5,1}
              decomposes as
            #eq:5dDecompositionof3Form.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                    %mo +
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_3
                    \\;=\;
                    \\widehat{F} \wedge d x^{5}
                    +
                    \\widehat{H}
            %p for unique differential forms of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi κ
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat F
                    \\;=\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}\hat F_{\kappa_1 \kappa_2}(x^\kappa, x^5)
                    d x^{\kappa_1} \wedge d x^{\kappa_2}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mn 3
                          %mo !
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo ^
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi κ
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 3
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat{H}
                    \\;=\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{3!} \widehat{H}_{\kappa_1 \kappa_2 \kappa_3}(x^\kappa, x^5)
                    d x^{\kappa_1} \wedge d x^{\kappa_2} \wedge d x^{\kappa_3}
                    \\,.
            %p
              In the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
              has vanishing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+derivative"} Lie derivative
              along the
              = succeed "-direction," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 5
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^5
            #eq:VanishingLieDerivateiveAlongx5.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mn 5
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{L}_5 H_3 \;=\; 0
            %p
              then also these components forms do not depend on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^5
              are actualls
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullbacks
              of differential forms on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 4
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{4,1}
            %p
              In terms of this decomposition, the 6d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+dual"} Hodge dual
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
              is equivalently given by the 5d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+duals"} Hodge duals
              of these components as (best seen by the relation to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+pairing"} Hodge pairing
              according to
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Hodge+star+operator#HodgePairing"} this Prop.
            #eq:6dHodgeDualityInTermsOf5d.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mn 6
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mn 5
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo ^
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mn 5
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\star_6 H_3
                    \\;=\;
                    \\big( \star_5 \widehat{H}\big) \wedge d x^{5}
                    \-
                    \\star_5 \widehat{F}
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+star+operator"} Hodge star operator
              squares to unity in the special case that it is applied to differential 3-forms on 6d Minkowski spacetime (by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Hodge+star+operator#HodgeStarFollowedByHodgeStar"} this Prop.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mn 6
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mn 6
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\star_6 \star_6 H_3 \;=\; + H_3
            %p
              we may ask for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
              to he
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+duality"} Hodge self-dual
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:6dHodgeDualityInTermsOf5d"} (3)
              this means equivalently that its 5d components are 5d Hodge duals of each other:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mn 6
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ⇔
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mn 3
                        %mo =
                        %mover
                          %mi F
                          %mo ^
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 5
                        %mo +
                        %mover
                          %mi H
                          %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo ^
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mn 5
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo ^
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    H_3
                    \\;=\;
                    \\star_{6} H_3
                    \\big)
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\overset{
                    H_3 = \widehat{F} \wedge d x^5 + \widehat{H}
                    }{
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    }
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\big(
                    \\widehat{H} = \star_5 \widehat{F}
                    \\big)
                    \\,.
            %p
              It follows that if there is no
              = succeed "-dependence" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 5
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^5
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VanishingLieDerivateiveAlongx5"} (2)
              then the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+differential+form"} closed
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual 3-form
              is equivalent to its 5d components
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
