            %p
              This may be summarized as saying that the massless part of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+reduction"} Kaluza-Klein reduction
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual 3-form theory
              from 6d to 5d is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Maxwell+theory"} D=5 Maxwell theory
            %p
              Essentially this relation underlies the formulation of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
              via the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Perry-Schwarz+Lagrangian"} Perry-Schwarz Lagrangian
          %h2#details Details
          %h3#ForTheFreeSelfDualField For the free self-dual field and trivial target space metric
          %p
            We review the definitions from
            %a{:href => "#PerrySchwarz96"} Perry-Schwarz 96, Section 2 “The Free Theory”
            (following
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#HenneauxTeitelboim88"} Henneaux-Teitelboim 88
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            of just the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+field"} self-dual higher gauge field
            on a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            for would-be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            being
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            In doing so, we translate to
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate
            = succeed "-formalism" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+calculus"} Cartan calculus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            on possibly non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+bundle"} trivial
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
          %h4#worldvolume_and_selfduality Worldvolume and self-duality
          %p Let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 6
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Sigma^6, g)
          %p
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            6 and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+of+a+quadratic+form"} signature
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-,+,+,+,+,+)
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
          %p
            In this dimension and with this signature, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+star+operator"} Hodge star operator
            squares to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+3-form"} differential 3-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 6
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H \;\in\; \Omega^3\big(\Sigma^6\big)
          %p
            the condition that it be self-dual (
            %a{:href => "#PerrySchwarz96"}> PS 96 (2)
            )
          #eq:SelfDualityIn6d.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
